I built the workflow and saved it to slot w4-rA. It passes the lint with no errors, and one test chat turn starts correctly: the agent says it is Freya Bank's digital assistant, that the call is recorded, and asks "Am I speaking with Ms Lee?". That was the only live test; there are no multi-turn chats and no practice cases, as instructed. Because of the time limit I did not do the separate rule-by-rule re-read of the brief.

- **Structure:** the date-facts code node runs first and passes to an opening node, then identity, then negotiation, then a hang-up node. The call only ends after `close_call` succeeds. The code node and the account hook are used as given.
- **Account lookup:** `get_account` is a tool inside the negotiation node, not a separate lookup node before it, so the account hook can run on it as the hook instructions require. The prompt tells the agent to call it first.
- **Deadlines:** they follow the 2026-10-09 amendment memo (12 business days for 1–7 days late, 7 for 8–45). The date facts already use these values, so nothing differs from the brief.
- **Promise failures:** the rule "try once more, then close as `no_promise` / `service_error`" is in the negotiation prompt and in the promise tool's result text. It is not enforced by a routing transition on the failure counters, so a model slip there is not caught.

